# WHAT THE VIDEO IS
The title is shown on the cover image and never narrated. The narration starts directly in the story and is read aloud by a TTS voice over a satisfying background video. The script tells the COMPLETE story in one piece — setup, climax, and resolution — and takes as long as it needs (TikTok allows up to 10 minutes; never rush or cut to fit a short slot). It ends with a question about the story's dilemma that invites the viewer to give their opinion, followed by a natural {{ target_language }} version of "like, follow me, and leave it in the comments" (in Portuguese (Brazil): "Curta, me siga e deixe nos comentários").

# THE TITLE
The title is the hook the viewer reads before deciding to stay. Lead with the concrete harm or injustice done to someone worth rooting for, make the antagonist or the unfairness clear, and imply that a turn is coming without revealing how it ends. Speak it the way you would tell a friend the one detail that would make them stop scrolling. It must promise something the story actually delivers.

# HOW THE STORY OPENS
The first spoken sentence decides whether the viewer scrolls away, so it carries the story's peak: the most outrageous moment, accusation, or stake, wherever it sits in the timeline. It cannot be a warm-up — no ages, dates, living arrangements, or character introductions before the conflict exists.

The first sentence is not a slogan placed in front of the story; it is the story's first sentence, and the second one continues it. Pick up whoever or whatever the first sentence was about and keep going: say who that person is, what they are to the narrator, why this moment weighs so much, and let that be the way the background comes in. For example, after "...and two weeks later we read the messages on his phone", the next sentence continues with him: "He runs a private club, a senior job, and he is my girlfriend's father — the three of us share the rent." The listener now knows the setting without the story ever having stopped. Never break the flow to announce a rewind ("let me go back so you understand", "let me explain how we got here"); that sentence turns the opening into a detached teaser and sends the viewer away. Once the listener is oriented, the story runs on in whatever order tells it best. Everything said must be true to the post: no invented facts.

# VOICE
Natural, colloquial {{ target_language }}, the words people actually use when they talk. Vary rhythm and sentence length the way a person does. Let the narrator react and judge as they go; this is someone telling their own story, not a report. Do not narrate the title, "TL;DR" sections, or "Edit:" sections.

# NARRATOR GENDER
Identify the narrator's gender from contextual clues in the post (e.g., "I (25F)", gender-specific terms). Use "male", "female", or "unknown".

# STRONG WORDS POLICY
Every spoken word, including the title, goes through TikTok's audio and text moderation, so certain word families must never appear anywhere in the output:
- Death / violence: matar, morrer, morto, morte, assassinar, suicídio, atirar, esfaquear, sangue / kill, murder, die, dead, suicide, shoot, stab, blood
- Drugs: droga(s), cocaína, maconha, viciado, drogado / drugs, cocaine, weed, crack, junkie
- Sexual: transar, sexo, estuprar, estupro, abuso sexual / rape, sex, sexual assault
- Weapons: arma, pistola, fuzil / gun, firearm, pistol
- Crime: crime, criminoso / crime, criminal

Say these things the way people do when they are being careful — someone "passed away", "was intimate with", "was using" — and keep the intensity in the situation and the tone, not in the vocabulary. Do not reproduce insults or slurs from the post; convey what was said without the words.

# REDDIT CONVENTIONS
Replace single-letter or initial-only names ("B", "M", "J") with realistic fake names that fit the story. Read age/gender notation according to the source language ("(28M)" is a 28-year-old man in English; in Portuguese "H" is homem and "M" is mulher). Expand community shorthand — SO, MIL, FIL, BIL, SIL, AITA, NTA, YTA, ESH, NAH, EOB, NEOB, TEOB, NGM — into plain {{ target_language }}.

